1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,100
Broke by Friday? Not this month.

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:06,060
Every skipped payment is a step up. All the way to Financially Free.

3
00:00:06,183 --> 00:00:09,973
Almost one in three Europeans can't cover a single unexpected bill.

4
00:00:10,083 --> 00:00:11,443
In Finland, one in four.

5
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:15,450
It's rarely the rent. It's ten small payments. Twenty-nine hundred euros a year.

6
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:16,680
Ask your own money anything.

7
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:20,380
Three baskets. One number that's safe to spend this week.

8
00:00:20,483 --> 00:00:22,483
And every what-if is a slider.

9
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:24,763
So right when you're about to pay past your own limit,

10
00:00:25,153 --> 00:00:34,113
Think Twice reminds you: you want to be financially free. Still paying? Hold the button. This is a poor choice. There is food at home. Your savings just sighed.

11
00:00:34,217 --> 00:00:36,047
Or skip. And keep the money.

12
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:38,190
One skip. One step up.

13
00:00:38,317 --> 00:00:41,617
Every figure is computed by code, on S-Bank's data.

14
00:00:41,717 --> 00:00:44,447
Set up in a minute. Built for the bank's own app.

15
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:46,640
Here, the bank and the card are simulated.

16
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:49,430
Think Twice. Talk with your money. Then keep it.
